      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I remarked this too - but a little bit different: It looks, like the \"Last updated\" date is only updated, when you are also listed in the \"Updated recently\" list. \n\nIf you do daily updates for example (which is usual, when your world is still in develeopment), then you will be blocked from this list (for a duration of 5 days or so). This makes probably sense, because some creators would use it to stay permanently on that list. But this blocking mechanism seems also to suppress the \"Last Update\" date, which is bad, in my opinion. Users should be able to see, if the world was updated.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
